WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
If you've been following my videos for the
last couple of weeks you will know that I am at

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.049
Disney World.

00:00:04.049 --> 00:00:07.450
It's not that they've sponsored me or anything, it is
just where I happen to be on holiday.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.570
Now, I've been avoiding Disney trivia

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.740
because, you know, it's a little bit
boring after a while but

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.289
there's something that my
cameraman for the week, Dan W,

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:21.890
-- Hello!
-- told me that I didn't really believe at first,

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:25.750
but he assures me it's true, I've looked it up, which is, well...

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.279
Dan, where are we currently standing?
DAN: We're at the Reedy Creek Improvement District. It's

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:32.430
Walt Disney World's own private
municipality.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.910
TOM: Yeah. Essentially, Disney World has private cities

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.309
granted to them by the state of Florida
because they lobbied a long time ago when

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:41.620
they were buying all the land here and buying the space.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.860
They have all sorts of powers: they apply for
planning permission

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.210
from themselves, they have the ability
to build all sorts of things, to

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.140
be immune from laws of the neighboring
areas that they would otherwise

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.489
be beholden to. Not only that, they have eminent domain,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:00.850
as well, which means that they can seize small
amounts of land from around their borders

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:03.949
for their own municipality if they need it for
the public good.

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:08.130
And the startling thing is this: Dan, what
they technically have permission to build?

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.390
DAN: They have planning permission from
themselves to build their own nuclear

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.200
power station. It's in the legislation
from the 1960s still.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.100
TOM: Now, that's because way back
when they were actually planning to build a proper city here.

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:23.170
And, while they've never actually built that
nuke plant – they have a small

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.250
oil-fired plant somewhere on property – 
they had their own

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.909
runway briefly, they had all sorts of things. 
There was gonna be a massive city here and then

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.600
Walt Disney died, and what we are left with
is the Experimental Prototype Community Of Tomorrow,

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:39.750
or EPCOT. But you never know, one day there might well be a nuclear power plant here

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.950
That is something

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.600
you might not have known.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.180
[Translating these subtitles? Add your name here!]

